+
+The [approved composition model](../PAGE.md) has useful current foundations and remaining platform work. This register identifies that difference without turning an example into a component inventory, schema, ABI or implementation schedule. Current observations below are bounded source inspections of the named producer/consumer paths, not product runtime tests or an exhaustive search proving that no other implementation exists. A gap stays open until its owning subsystem demonstrates the intended end-to-end capability.
+
+## PP-G01 — Component host and contributions
+
+**Target:** A useful standard presentation library supports configuration and declarative composition, with specialized protected plugin contributions through a defined host. Portable components receive explicit data, identity and actions; registration grants no ambient store, network, database or service authority. Canonical file-type rendering retains its platform owner.
+
+**Current limit and evidence strength:** `ContentArea.tsx` dispatches fixed built-in IDs to React components. `componentTabLauncherCatalog.ts` has two code-owned launcher entries, `capture.home` and `file.open`, consumed through connected-owner bindings. These are inspected static dispatch and closed-launcher foundations, not evidence of a general installed-plugin contribution host. See [Platform Boundaries](../../001-Platform_Boundaries/PAGE.md#current-source-inspected-foundation) and [Composable Presentation](../../003-Composable_Presentation/PAGE.md#current-source-inspected-foundation).
+
+**Remaining capability:** Define and implement contribution registration, explicit supported inputs/actions, compatibility and execution/isolation under the protected host boundary. **Owner:** UI, platform and plugin subsystems. **Decision trigger:** Resolve PP-O02 before loading contributed executable components; resolve PP-O06 before selecting the initial library, first conversion and rollout. Arbitrary in-process React imports are not a chosen contract.
+
+## PP-G02 — Shell and canonical file reuse
+
+**Target:** Collections can ask the shell to open the canonical file surface in the current tab with a return route or in another tab. Shell identity, focus and lifecycle, collection selection/filter/navigation, file presentation/editing and service-owned save/history keep their respective owners.
+
+**Current limit and evidence strength:** `componentTabConnectedOwner.ts` delegates collection reads and applies to explicit owner ports. The Files ports use `fileStore.ts` and its connected-tab action; `ComponentTabPanel.tsx` resolves content through a supplied resolver, while the file target helper supplies code-owned identity to Files placement. This source trace demonstrates specific connected ownership, not generalized reuse across plugin collections, drawers and windows. [Tabs, Drawers And Files](../../004-Tabs_Drawers_And_Files/PAGE.md#current-source-inspected-foundation) explains that foundation.
+
+**Remaining capability:** Generalize the approved collection/file/return flow through established host and file owners, with explicit content inputs and actions. Do not add a second tab store or alternate save implementation. **Owner:** shell/tab hosts, collection owners and canonical file surface. **Decision trigger:** Resolve PP-O02 host mechanics and PP-O06 first conversion before rollout; decide any new duplicate-tab, dirty-buffer, restoration or close policy before changing that behavior, preserving existing owner rules meanwhile. Chat placement remains governed by [Chat's side-chat decision](../../../007-Chat_System/000-Overview_and_References/002-Decisions/PAGE.md#2026-09-19--side-chat-tabs-and-non-chat-windows).
+
+## PP-G03 — Hybrid custom-region interface
+
+**Target:** Standard host pieces can sit beside specialized iframe UI, with narrow authorized requests to platform operations. An iframe-side standard UI library remains optional and deferred.
+
+**Current limit and evidence strength:** `ContentArea.tsx` has separate local-app/custom branches. `CustomViewer.tsx` passes a local-server URL through `IframeSurface` to `FrameElement`; the navigation hook cannot enforce its changed-origin comparison when a cross-origin location read fails. This establishes embedding, not a general hybrid bridge, SDK or complete isolation model. See [Custom Iframe Composition](../../006-Custom_Iframe_Composition/PAGE.md#current-source-inspected-embedding).
+
+**Remaining capability:** Define the host/custom-region operation boundary, identity, authorization, supported operations and failure behavior without granting unrestricted server, Node, filesystem or database access. **Owner:** platform and custom-view subsystems. **Decision trigger:** Resolve PP-O05 transport and authorization/isolation choices before shipping the bridge or optional SDK. An iframe element or copied configuration supplies neither interface nor capability authority.
+
+## PP-G04 — External-store mediation
+
+**Target:** Authorized owning commands/adapters operate on application files, separate SQLite/CSV/JSON stores and connected services; outcome facts describe actual transitions and the bus distributes them. System storage remains platform-owned.
+
+**Current limit and evidence strength:** The inspected mediated-save controller prepares required operation/preimage protection before replacement, then handles resource-fact publication through `fact-replay.js` separately from the write outcome. `admission.js` seals four trusted publisher identities for save and agent observations. This bounded producer/consumer path is not a general external-store mutation API or plugin publisher factory; it does not prove cross-store atomicity. [Data And Actions](../../005-Data_And_Actions/PAGE.md#current-source-inspected-save-boundary) supplies the trace and limits.
+
+**Remaining capability:** Define each adapter's authorization, mutation result, retry/transaction and provenance/recovery integration. Preserve the distinction between required prewrite protection, optional reported context, postwrite recovery and post-tool observation under [Events And Ledger decisions](../../../010-Events_And_Ledger/000-Events_And_Ledger/002-Decisions/PAGE.md). **Owner:** data-operation/adapter and provenance subsystems. **Decision trigger:** Resolve PP-O07 before exposing general external-store mutation APIs; plugin emission and permission grammar remain subject to the event owner's general-plugin gate. A logged tool call is not proof of a successful write.
+
+## Workspace gaps keep their existing owners
+
+The [workspace and view register](../../../001-Workspaces_And_Views/000-Workspaces_And_Views/003-Unfinished_Work/PAGE.md) remains authoritative for [WV-G02 provisioning](../../../001-Workspaces_And_Views/000-Workspaces_And_Views/003-Unfinished_Work/PAGE.md#wv-g02--plugin-aware-composition-and-provisioning), [WV-G03 repeatable instances](../../../001-Workspaces_And_Views/000-Workspaces_And_Views/003-Unfinished_Work/PAGE.md#wv-g03--repeatable-instances-of-a-view-plugin), [WV-G04 local agent context](../../../001-Workspaces_And_Views/000-Workspaces_And_Views/003-Unfinished_Work/PAGE.md#wv-g04--view-local-agent-context) and [WV-G05 editable placement/capability binding](../../../001-Workspaces_And_Views/000-Workspaces_And_Views/003-Unfinished_Work/PAGE.md#wv-g05--editable-instance-placement-and-capability-binding). Their status is not duplicated here. The settled local orientation and manual cross-view reads do not close the harness-specific context mechanics gap.
+
+[Platform decisions](../001-Decisions/PAGE.md#open-choices-and-decision-gates) collect the open choices and their triggers. Specialist Wiki, Voice, Chat and event references remain available under their own owners; these platform observations do not recertify those domains or authorize product implementation.
